-- title:
--   Geometric closed fibres of the two-chart model of X₁(Mp)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M\ge 5$ with $p\nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a $\{p\}$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta\in L$, and an intermediate field $K$ of $L\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ assumed equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the image of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ under coefficientwise base change. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with $A$ acting on $K$ compatibly with $L$, and let $j\in K$ be a nonzero element whose image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ is the coefficient embedding of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). The assertion is: for every algebraically closed field $k$ and every ring homomorphism $f\colon A\to k$ with $\ker f\ne\bot$, there exist schemes $C_1,C_2$ with morphisms $c_i\colon C_i\to\operatorname{Spec} k$ that are proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, morphisms $i_\nu\colon C_\nu\to X_k$ into the fibre $X_k=\;$the pullback of [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) along $\operatorname{Spec} f$ satisfying $i_\nu$ followed by the second projection equals $c_\nu$, both closed immersions, a natural number $n$, and two-chart affine open covers of $C_1$ and of $C_2$ (each being a pair of affine opens with affine intersection whose union is everything), such that $X_k$ is reduced, every point of $X_k$ lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$ on underlying spaces, and the fibre product of $i_1$ and $i_2$ is reduced with exactly $n$ points, where $n>0$.
--
--   This is the geometric description of the closed fibres of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over a discrete valuation ring containing $\zeta_p$: each such fibre is reduced and is the union of two proper smooth geometrically integral curves meeting in a nonempty finite reduced scheme. It is packaged exactly in the shape required by the classification of relative sub-Picard data, and is used in the descent of Hecke-generated classes and in the construction of homomorphisms classifying pullbacks of the Poincaré bundle at the two-chart model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_exists_twoGluedSmoothCurves_isReduced_pullback_twoChartModel_x1_mul_of_ker_ne_bot.lean

